# scratch/ is untracked working space. Two CF-93 analysis-probe directories are
# deliberately TRACKED so the measurements in decision-log.md 2026-07-25 § the
# CF-93 round-1 per-class matrix entry stay reproducible — that entry could only
# be authored because the -21 probe SOURCE survived. `scratch/*` (contents), not
# `scratch/` (the directory): git cannot re-include a child of an excluded dir.
# These are ANALYSIS SCRIPTS, not tests — outside every package's src, so they
# enter no lint / typecheck / vitest gate and are excluded from Rule 13.
scratch/*
!scratch/cf93-p21/
!scratch/cf93-p23/
!scratch/cf93-p25/
!scratch/cf95-recipe-ladder/
# cf93-p25 tracks the CDP visual-verification harness SCRIPTS only. Its captured
# PNGs are deliberately NOT tracked — they are large, regenerable by re-running
# the harness, and Rule 38 asks for the reproduction path, not the output.
scratch/cf93-p25/*.png
scratch/cf93-p25/chrome-profile/
# cf95-recipe-ladder is the recipe-ladder visual harness; same rule — scripts
# tracked, captures and the browser profile not. Its driver reuses cf93-p25's
# cdp.mjs rather than duplicating it, so that directory is a hard dependency.
scratch/cf95-recipe-ladder/*.png
scratch/cf95-recipe-ladder/*.json
scratch/cf95-recipe-ladder/chrome-profile/
